  <h1>About pregnancydiscriminationcalc.com</h1>
  <p>pregnancydiscriminationcalc.com is a free employment law resource maintained by The Click Lab. Our damages calculator and guides help pregnant and postpartum workers understand what the Pregnancy Discrimination Act, Title VII, and the Pregnant Workers Fairness Act actually protect, recognize the patterns that suggest pregnancy played a role in a termination, demotion, or denied accommodation, and get a plain-English starting estimate of potential recovery &mdash; before the EEOC filing clock runs out.</p>

  <p>pregnancydiscriminationcalc.com is a free employment law resource maintained by The Click Lab. Our calculator and guides help workers understand pregnancy discrimination damages, the legal frameworks that apply, and the practical steps involved in pursuing a claim under the Pregnancy Discrimination Act, Title VII, the Pregnant Workers Fairness Act, and related federal and state laws.</p>

  <h2>What We Do</h2>
  <p>We translate complex employment law concepts into plain-English calculators and guides that anyone can use without a law degree. The damages calculator on this site estimates potential recovery from a pregnancy discrimination or PWFA accommodation failure claim, drawing on the Title VII damages caps, back pay and front pay formulas, and the evidentiary standards courts apply to compensatory and punitive damage claims. Every formula is documented on the <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a>.</p>
  <p>Our guides cover the full landscape of pregnancy discrimination law: what types of conduct are prohibited, how Title VII damages are structured, what the PWFA adds beyond the PDA, how to file an EEOC charge and preserve your rights, and what common misconceptions cause workers to underestimate the strength of their claims. Every guide is reviewed by our editorial team before publication and updated when the law changes.</p>

  <h2>What We Don't Do</h2>
  <p>We do not provide legal advice, and nothing on this site creates an attorney-client relationship. The calculator produces estimates based on the inputs you provide and the formulas described in our methodology. Actual results in litigation depend on the specific facts, the strength of the evidence, the forum, the judge and jury, and many other variables that no calculator can predict. For guidance on your specific situation, consult a licensed employment attorney. Many employment attorneys take pregnancy discrimination cases on contingency and offer free initial consultations.</p>

  <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
  <p>This site is supported by display advertising through Google AdSense. We do not sell reader data, accept sponsored content, or receive compensation from law firms or any other advertisers in exchange for editorial coverage. Our editorial team operates independently of our advertising relationships.</p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>For corrections, feedback, or media inquiries, see our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. For information about our editorial process and team credentials, see the <a href="/editorial">editorial page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
